\n$$\n\nIn general, for a complex number\n\n$$\nz=a+b\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nthe magnitude of $z$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\mid z \\mid = \\sqrt{a^2+b^2}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055976 #edb/ref 1065 3329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055976 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "df0d2109-2954-5b2d-8b02-98a43f80ac89" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055976 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068678 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068678 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068678 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068678 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069296 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068678 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Length of the Hypotenuse of a Given Right Triangle" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068678 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068678 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b6db510b-5976-5c90-8e02-b9f61ff3327b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068679 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068679 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068679 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186459302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068679 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186480701 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068679 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186487374 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068679 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186489178 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068679 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186491172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068679 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186498515 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068679 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186555823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068679 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Length of the Hypotenuse Given the Length of the Legs of a Right Triangle" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068679 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068540 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068679 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid